<div class="entity entity--full">
  <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="small mb-2"><a href="/data/">Data</a> › SPARQL query</nav>
  <h1 class="mb-3">SPARQL query</h1>
  <div class="reading-column ms-0">
    <p>Write a SPARQL query against the released LOD-AM data and run it here, or start from one of the
    <a href="/query/examples/">example queries</a>. The data follow the
    <a href="https://github.com/LOD-AM/knowledge-graph/blob/main/CONVENTIONS.md">LOD-AM conventions</a>.</p>
    <p class="small text-body-secondary">Endpoint: <code>{{ metadata.sparqlEndpoint }}</code> (read-only; queries stop after 120 seconds).
    Nothing is sent before you run a query. When you do, your browser sends the query to <code>triple.lod-am.net</code>,
    the LOD-AM triplestore. The editor keeps nothing in your browser after you leave the page.
    Details: <a href="/privacy/#sparql">privacy policy, section 4</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <noscript><p class="data-box series-box">The editor needs JavaScript. Without it, you can send queries to the endpoint
  directly, e.g. <code>curl --data-urlencode query@query.rq {{ metadata.sparqlEndpoint }}</code>, or read the
  <a href="/query/examples/">example queries</a>.</p></noscript>

  <div id="yasgui" class="lodam-yasgui mt-4" data-endpoint="{{ metadata.sparqlEndpoint }}"
       data-default-query="{{ exampleQueries[0].query }}"></div>
</div>
